Plan: 
    We need the GameBoard, then cards and score. I think the cards and just be in the board without being wrapped up in anything else. Each card can be assigned an image on run and then the order of the cards can be shuffled around. They can be simply stored in a list and then the list shuffled at each go. We don't have to worry about the shuffling part now. We can start with the easy stuff

    So the Gameboard needs to contain the container that hosts the cards. It, in CSS, would control the layout. We can simply create an arbitrarily long array of cards, which for now can just contain a colored div so that we can arrage the cards on the screen.

    I guess we need to find an API to get images and names from of some kind. 

    We need a to match up the cards. I'm guessing it's easy enough to just keep a list of the cards that have been chosen. Each time we choose a card, we check the list to see if it has already been picked. If not, then we add it to the list. If it has, then we need to check if the current score is greater than the best score. if it is, then we assign it the new best score. We could just do that each turn actually. 

    What we don't really know yet is how to arrange the original photos. First we need some photos to arrange. And the project wants us to do an API call with useEffect. It doesn't exactly seem necessary? But it is possible I suppose. Should we just focus on the logic first with static images, then add in the useEffect stuff after? 

